      "$comment": "R9: arrow functions become every() sentences. A binder (every, any, first) takes an imported placeholder and is followed by in(list); everything after that in() is inside the every() sentence, where participles, -ing forms and is()-actions are allowed (R1, R4) and the copy is said as to().clone() (R5). `starts` is the first word of each sentence and the one kind of result it decides. `bodyAtoms` are the body words, one atom each; a body is exactly one of them. `sentences` is the R9 table and `nested` the nested callbacks (every(y).in(x)), each with its plain-JS twin; test/fluent.test.mjs runs both, test/grammar.test.mjs holds them to the rules.",
